From: gf691271 <gf691271@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:20:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: unsigned single-byte samples; retry the blob through the
 morning

Four items from the review, each verified or explicitly not verified.

1. HEART_RATE / SPO / RESTING_HEART_RATE were read as signed bytes.

   FitnessData.StepResponse.parseData assigns `value = data[i++]` (byte -> short) for the
   single-byte tags, and the second bitmap does the same (`byte value = data[i++]`). A heart
   rate of 130 (0x82) therefore became -126. Not theoretical: HUAWEI_ACTIVITY_SAMPLE on the
   test device held -127/-124/-116/-109, i.e. 129/132/140/147 bpm, and its maximum was 125
   because everything above 127 had been flipped. STEPS was already correct (two-byte path
   masks both bytes).

   Both sites now mask with 0xFF. TestFitnessDataSignHandling covers below-127, above-127,
   0xFF, SpO2, resting HR and the parsedData value; 4 tests, all pass
   (`testMainlineDebugUnitTest --tests *TestFitnessDataSignHandling*`).

2. The raw sleep_state file is archived. Each segment is 16 bytes and the parser uses only
   the first 8 (start, end); the other 8 have never been stored, so they could not be studied.
   Saved next to the dumps as sleep_state_<epoch_ms>.bin.

3. The blob is retried through the morning. On 2026-11-17 the session ended at 08:11 and the
   08:00 periodic sync had already asked and received size 0; the night only survived because
   a human reconnected at 08:58. Now an empty dump between 07:00 and 13:00 schedules another
   attempt an hour later, up to 6 times.

4. Manifests from an older schema are moved out of the `manifest-*.json` glob when the schema
   is bumped: `export_schema.txt` remembers what this exporter last wrote, and the old files
   are renamed to `manifest-<stamp>.json.v<old>.stale`. Not device-verified yet.

Compiled: assembleMainlineDebug BUILD_OK. Unit test green. Not installed: the device dropped
off adb during the install.
